      "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nTurns on `automatic_shard` for two long NVIDIA steps and six AMD mirrors that run longer than 20 minutes as one job. Picked by p90 duration over the last day on main. Only the flag changes; no commands or tests change.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Each step below runs as parallel jobs planned from main's per-file timings, and each job runs only its share of the tests:\n\n| Step | Command shape | Planned shards |\n|---|---|---:|\n| `e2e-scheduling-1-gpu` | one `pytest` file, split by test | 2 |\n| `amd-e2e-scheduling-1-gpu` (mirror) | same | 2 |\n| `benchmarks-cli-test` | one `pytest` over `benchmarks/` | 2 |\n| `amd-kernels-root-misc-test-b200` (mirror) | one `pytest` over a list of kernel test files, with `--deselect` | 2 |\n| `amd-spec-decode-eagle-nightly-b200` (optional mirror) | one `pytest` over a directory; its large file is split by test | 2 |\n| `amd-spec-decode-speculators-mtp-nightly-b200` (optional mirror) | two `pytest` commands over directories | 2 |\n| `amd-lm-eval-large-models-ep-2xb200` (optional mirror) | `export` setup, then `pytest` on the gsm8k eval with `--config-list-file`, split by test | 2 |\n| `amd-lm-eval-large-models-4xh100` (optional mirror) | `export` setup, then `pytest` on the lm-eval harness test with `--config-list-file` and `--tp-size`, split by test | 2 |\n\n- `kernels-root-misc-test-b200`, `spec-decode-eagle-nightly-b200` and `spec-decode-speculators-mtp-nightly-b200` are enrolled so their mirrors can shard (a mirror shards only when its base step is enrolled). Their own runs plan to one shard, so they stay one job.\n- Every test runs exactly once across the shards, with the same environment as the single job. If planning fails, the step runs as one job, as it does today.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Planned each step on this branch with ci-infra's `runtime_shard.plan_step`, using main's timings on the step's own queue.\n- Rendered each step with the pipeline generator and ran every shard's commands against a mock test tree, as a PR build and with main's `pytest -p ci_otel` wrapper. Every test ran in exactly one shard, with the same env. The three single-shard base steps were confirmed to stay one job.\n- `/ci run` exercises E2E Scheduling, Benchmarks CLI and the E2E Scheduling and Miscellaneous Kernels mirrors. The four optional mirrors need a build scoped to their keys.\n\n## Details\n\n- **Uneven or tight plans.** `amd-lm-eval-large-models-ep-2xb200`'s planner output is marked over budget: one eval test takes most of 20 minutes by itself, so its slowest shard sits near the target.\n- **Left out.**\n  - `language-models-test-extended-generation` and its mirror: each job first builds mamba-ssm and causal-conv1d from source, which every shard would repeat. They wait for #58795, which prebuilds both in the test image.\n  - `entrypoints-integration-api-server-generate`'s mirror: two of its files assert on `caplog`, the pattern that took `entrypoints-integration-multimodal` out of sharding.\n  - `benchmarks-cli-test`'s mirror runs under 20 minutes, so it stays one job.\n  - Long steps whose commands aren't plain pytest (PyTorch Fullgraph, NixlConnector PD accuracy, Examples, Spec Decode MTP + Other) can't be planned.\n- **Where to look.** The `automatic_shard: true` lines in `.buildkite/test_areas/{engine,benchmarks,kernels,spec_decode,lm_eval}.yaml`.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
